From 7a320e5389a4238017322d02718d1814599ca4d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 21:07:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Publish CLI discovery: live-link 0.1.0 on npm and the public
 skill

Flip registry.distribution to published for live-link 0.1.0 with the
install command and the skill install line, drop Public CLI installation
from the unavailable list, and show the install commands in the CLI README.
Every guide, llms.txt, agent.json and the CLI help now render the
published variant; the unpublished variant remains tested through the
registry override.

Add the published-cli CI job: it runs the pinned package from a clean
directory and verifies npm metadata, tarball bytes, public tag, skill and
notices against this source. The job is red until the pin exists on npm,
which is the merge gate. The bundled CLI inlines the registry, so this
commit is also the release commit: tag its head cli-v0.1.0, let the tag
workflow publish, re-run CI, then merge (docs/operations/CLI_RELEASE.md).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017twst4MFpEXdY2hjihXFdf
