 ## Release
 
-From `main` at the reviewed commit, with `packages/cli/package.json` and `packages/cli/src/version.mjs`
-agreeing on the pin:
-
-```sh
-pnpm release:build
-node scripts/release/verify-distribution.mjs --dry-run dist/distribution     # must print ok: true
-git tag cli-v0.1.0 && git push origin cli-v0.1.0
-```
-
-`release-cli.yml` rebuilds and re-verifies on the runner, then pushes the tree and tag `v0.1.0` to the
-skill repository. Its `publish.yml` verifies every file hash and mode again, smoke-tests the bundle,
-and publishes to npm with provenance. A tag that already exists in the skill repository fails the
-release; bump the pin instead of re-tagging.
-
-## Verify the published release
-
-```sh
-node scripts/release/verify-distribution.mjs 0.1.0            # npm metadata, tag, skill, notices, tarball bytes
-npx -y live-link@0.1.0 doctor                                  # from a clean container, no repository checkout
-npx skills add Melade-Inc/live-link-skill --skill live-link --list
-```
-
-All three must pass before the flip.
-
-## Flip discovery to published
-
-Merge the prepared "publish CLI discovery" change: `registry.distribution` becomes
-`{ status: 'published', version: '0.1.0', install: 'npx -y live-link@0.1.0', skill: 'npx skills add …' }`,
-`Public CLI installation` leaves the `unavailable` list, and CI gains the `published-cli` job that runs
-the pinned package from the registry. Deploy management; confirm `https://live.link/start.md` and
-`/.well-known/agent.json` show the install command. The flip PR cannot merge before publication: its
-CI job fails while the pin is not on npm.
+The bundled CLI inlines the registry, so the published artifact must be built from the same source
+that declares it published. The release commit is therefore the flip commit:
+
+1. Open the "publish CLI discovery" PR: `registry.distribution` becomes
+   `{ status: 'published', version: '0.1.0', install: 'npx -y live-link@0.1.0', skill: 'npx skills add …' }`,
+   `Public CLI installation` leaves `unavailable`, CI gains the `published-cli` job, and the CLI README
+   shows the install commands. Its `published-cli` job is red until the pin exists; that is the gate.
+2. On that PR's head commit, run the dry run and tag:
+   ```sh
+   pnpm release:build
+   node scripts/release/verify-distribution.mjs --dry-run dist/distribution     # must print ok: true
+   git tag cli-v0.1.0 <pr-head-sha> && git push origin cli-v0.1.0
+   ```
+   `release-cli.yml` rebuilds and re-verifies on the runner, then pushes the tree and tag `v0.1.0` to
+   the skill repository, whose `publish.yml` verifies every file hash and mode, smoke-tests the bundle
+   and publishes to npm with provenance. A tag that already exists there fails the release; bump the
+   pin instead of re-tagging.
+3. Verify the published release from the same commit:
+   ```sh
+   node scripts/release/verify-distribution.mjs 0.1.0            # npm metadata, tag, skill, notices, tarball bytes
+   npx -y live-link@0.1.0 doctor                                  # clean container, no checkout
+   npx skills add Melade-Inc/live-link-skill --skill live-link --list
+   ```
+4. Re-run the PR's CI; `published-cli` now passes. Squash-merge (the tree is identical to the tagged
+   commit, so the verifier keeps matching). Deploy management; confirm `https://live.link/start.md`
+   and `/.well-known/agent.json` show the install command and `skill`.
 
 ## Rollback
 
